# The Gradle wrapper is committed, contrary to the Flutter template.
#
# Flutter ignores gradlew, gradlew.bat and gradle-wrapper.jar by
# default, which means a fresh checkout cannot build the Android app at
# all -- CI failed on exactly that. Gradle's own guidance is the
# opposite: the wrapper belongs in the repository so every checkout,
# on every machine, builds with the same Gradle version.
#
# The jar is a binary, so CI verifies its checksum against Gradle's
# published releases before running it.

/.gradle
/captures/
/local.properties
GeneratedPluginRegistrant.java
.cxx/

# Remember to never publicly share your keystore.
# See https://flutter.dev/to/reference-keystore
key.properties
**/*.keystore
**/*.jks
